            <ArticleTitle>Responding to child sexual abuse disclosure.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>18-26</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/01.NPR.0000526762.68595.a1</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In cases of child sexual abuse (CSA), NPs are faced with a variety of options dictated by community, agency, and individual resources. This article looks at victim-centered care from current guidelines and offers resources for clinical practice decision making when responding to CSA disclosure.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
